title: The Other Parties
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/cards/other_parties.jpg
tags: party_affairs
view-if: other_parties_timer <= 0
on-arrival: other_parties_timer = 4; month_actions += 1

= The Other Parties

Labour has no majority. Every vote in the Commons depends on the Liberals, the nationalists and the Ulster Unionists. If we want to bring the government down, or govern in a hung parliament, we will need some of them.

- @liberals: Talk to David Steel's Liberals.
- @unionists: Cultivate the Ulster Unionists.
- @snp: Open a channel to the SNP.
- @plaid: Talk to Plaid Cymru.
- @electoral_reform: Promise the Liberals a Speaker's Conference on electoral reform.
- @easy_discard

@liberals
on-arrival: lib_relation += 8 if lib_lab_pact = 0; lib_relation += 4 if lib_lab_pact = 1; wet_dissent -= 2; dry_dissent += 2

[? if lib_lab_pact : While the Pact lasts, Steel is polite but committed to [+ prime_minister +]. ?][? if not lib_lab_pact : With the Pact over, Steel is free to listen. ?]

@unionists
on-arrival: uup_relation += 8; uup_relation += 4 if neave_dead = 0; right_dissent -= 2

[? if neave_dead = 0 : Airey Neave, who knows the Unionist MPs well, carries our messages. ?][? if neave_dead = 1 : Without Airey Neave, the conversations are harder going. ?] The Unionists want more Northern Irish seats at Westminster and a firm line on security.

@snp
on-arrival: snp_relation += 8 if devolution_stance >= 1; snp_relation += 4 if devolution_stance = 0; right_dissent += 3

The SNP's eleven MPs have no love for us, but they have even less for a Labour government that fails to deliver devolution.

@plaid
on-arrival: pc_relation += 6

Plaid's three MPs are mostly interested in Welsh questions, slate quarrymen's compensation in particular. We listen politely.

@electoral_reform
view-if: electoral_reform_promise = 0 and con_in_government = 0
subtitle: The Liberals would be delighted. Almost everyone in our own party would be furious.
on-arrival: electoral_reform_promise = 1; lib_relation += 15; right_dissent += 8; dry_dissent += 5; loyalist_dissent += 5

You promise that a Conservative government would at least look at proportional representation. In private, the party that has done well out of first-past-the-post for a century is aghast.
